From: beardedeagle <randy@heroictek.com>
Subject: [PATCH] fix(daemon): serialize stale instance record takeovers safely

Guard stale record takeover with immutable, generation-specific owner entries.
Reclamation and release unlink only the observed claim and remove directories
only when empty, so an old observer cannot rename or delete a new live guard.
Encode host/PID/creation identity in each claim name to protect in-progress
publication. Retain legacy stale guard, empty guard and crashed-owner recovery.

Preserve initial atomic publication and denied-unlink/rename recovery. Keep
in-place UTF-8 writes complete and truncate by byte length. Cover competing
processes with both a stale instance and stale guard, replacement-owner release,
crashed claims, denied-unlink recovery and complete non-ASCII records.

